# SP13 step 1: the benchmark sends 1,000 events and works out p50 and p95 from
# the rows the stack wrote.
# Format: file | regular expression the file must contain | message if it doesn't
scripts/bench.sh | COUNT=\$\{1:-1000\} | must default to 1,000 events
scripts/bench.sh | evt-\$i\.json | must build one event file per event
scripts/bench.sh | --recursive | must upload the whole folder in one call
scripts/bench.sh | --select COUNT | must poll the table's count until the rows land, inside a bounded loop
scripts/bench.sh | fromdateiso8601 | must turn the ISO timestamps into epoch seconds
scripts/bench.sh | capture\(" | must read the milliseconds separately, because fromdateiso8601 rejects them
scripts/bench.sh | p50= | must report p50
scripts/bench.sh | p95= | must report p95
scripts/bench.sh | evidence/bench-aws-raw\.json | must save the raw rows the numbers came from
